{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788264326,"nonce":"8lMYArS/isWrCSjqzjz5tmtw2o0=","message":"The promotion pass this spec was missing is now landed — session 13, on branch `s13-checklists`, merged to main.\n\n**The gap, stated plainly:** 4.4 had a retirement pass and no promotion pass, so the checklists could only ever SHRINK. Nothing ever moved a repeated observation up into an item.\n\nMeasured consequence in M1 run `m1-20260831`: the run FAILed `item-ids-known` on three ledger ids — `barracks-heat`, `postmortem-trigger`, `time-control-drift`. Session 12 invented all three mid-run for real observations that had nowhere to go: a room overheating, a death requiring a post-mortem, and losing time control. Those are not noise; they are exactly the promotion candidates 4.4 had no machinery to collect.\n\n**What landed** (`ba2ce65`), in `checklists/README.md` §The promotion pass:\n- Candidates are COMPUTED from the ledger, not swept for: ledger ids with no `### \u003cid\u003e` behind them — checks a run invented mid-flight because it needed one.\n- Two occasions promotes; each candidate is landed **or rejected in writing**, never dropped silently.\n- A promoted item lands at its moment class under the same cap and ladder as any other item.\n- \"A lesson no checklist cites\" is a second candidate class — which makes finding L (all four M1 lessons orphaned) a grep from here on instead of a sweep.\n- Promotion is the cheap direction to be wrong in: retirement undoes it off the next run's rows. That asymmetry is the reason the bar is two occasions rather than something stricter.\n\n`postmortem.md`'s demotion paragraph gained the uphill half so the two passes read as one mechanism.\n\n**The three ids were then promoted under it** (`2c98a45`), and this is the part worth reviewing against 4.4's cap rule: `barracks-heat` → `daily.md` as the **5th of 7**, under cap, so no merge-or-retire was owed. `postmortem-trigger` and `time-control-drift` → `triggered.md` events. **No incident class was added** — the ledger's id space is already closed by `accept/4.2-play-loop.py`'s `item-ids-known` and its verdict enum `{ok, action, blocked, n/a}`, so a run-level incident class would either fail the audit or fork a second, unaudited ledger. Each of the three already had a moment class in the existing grammar: heat is slow event-less drift, a death and a lost time control are events.\n\n`item-ids-known` FAILed on the M1 run before this branch and PASSes after.\n\nLeaving this issue OPEN: 4.4's rwtest-assertion rung still needs 5.1, and the retirement pass's N-run window is still unexercised — no run has yet been retired against.","files":null}]}